      "situation": "The bank payment journey has recovered. The last two recovery checks ran clean, the final one at 51 s.",
      "background": "About 13 s before the incident was raised, a pipeline change set payments max_transfer_minor from 1000000 to 1, so every payment was rejected with '422 amount exceeds transfer limit'. Around the same time the screening primary slowed to p95 1826 ms (baseline 15 ms), and clearing exited once with exit code 15.",
      "assessment": "The incident commander reverted payments max_transfer_minor to 1000000, which stopped the limit rejections. It failed screening over to its standby, which ended the 1.0 s screening timeouts and 503s, and it restarted clearing, which has stayed up since. Clearing's exit code 15 is a termination signal with no errors in its log, so the cause of that stop is not known.",
      "recommendation": "Find out why the pipeline set max_transfer_minor to 1, and block that change from being reapplied. Fix the slow screening primary before failing back from screening-standby, and find what sent the termination signal to clearing. Operations should review the payments rejected by the limit and those that failed with 503 screening timeouts during the incident, and confirm which ones need resubmitting."
    },
